"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nAfter studying at a nearby cafe for a bit, I looked for a restaurant nearby to have dinner.  \nMaybe because the weather had been hot for a few days, I didn't particularly feel like eating anything.  \nAfter debating for a long time, I decided to go for Dakgalbi as a safe choice, so I looked for a nearby Dakgalbi restaurant.  \n\nI didn't know it, but apparently it is a famous franchise.  \nWhen I looked it up, the head store seemed to be in Uijeongbu.  \n\nI ordered 2 servings of the most standard Dakgalbi and added ramen noodles.  \nI debated for a while between the traditional udon noodles and ramen, but ended up choosing ramen noodles.  \n\nI thought about ordering a Makguksu too, but decided to make up my mind after eating first.  \n\nAfter waiting a little, the Dakgalbi came out fully cooked.  \nThere were reviews saying the portion was large, and indeed, it was a lot.  \nAs I get older, I can't eat as much as before, but even considering that, the portion was not small.  \n\nThe taste was just typical Dakgalbi.  \nIt wasn't exceptionally delicious or bad; it was just a decent, average taste.  \n\nBy the time I finished eating, I was so full that I couldn't even make fried rice, and in the end, I couldn't eat Makguksu either.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"